[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1718945814","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2121#issuecomment-1718945814","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2121","id":1718945814,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85mdQgW","user":{"login":"n8willis","id":2192132,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTIxMzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2192132?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/n8willis","html_url":"https://github.com/n8willis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n8willis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n8willis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n8willis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n8willis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n8willis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n8willis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n8willis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n8willis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n8willis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-09-14T07:54:14Z","updated_at":"2023-09-14T07:54:14Z","body":"Definite +1 on *some* license regarding this font. It is used as the upstream for multiple other FOSS font projects, so tracking and preserving the source is crucial. \r\n\r\nHowever, I think there are some serious unresolved issues to be tackled with the license name, identifier, and the text itself.\r\n\r\nFirst, the license text. I looked into this a few years ago (2018?). To the best of my recollection of that research, there have been three separate licenses used. The original license granted permission from Adobe for the Utopia font to the X Consortium. That seems to be what the text linked to is. In Debian, it was considered ambiguous regarding whether it permitted modification (https://tug.org/pipermail/texhax/2005-September/004678.html) ... after which a new license was applied, by Adobe, to the TeX Users Group (TUG). That license / grant / etc was specific to TUG, but permitted sublicensing. TUG then sublicensed it for general public usage.\r\n\r\nThe summary of some of this stuff is actually fairly well linked on Wikipedia, so I won't repeat it all here: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Utopia_(typeface)\r\n\r\nI recall that I did find a more direct reference to the original X Consortium grant/statement/promise but I don't have that info in front of me and don't have the time at present.\r\n\r\nI don't take a position as to whether all three licenses need inclusion, but the third one (TUG->public) is more relevant in general, and yet this one (Adobe->XC) is surely necessary to traverse the graph getting to the third one.\r\n\r\nRegardless, \"Adobe Typeface\" seems to be an ambiguous name; the license was specific to the Utopia font and Adobe has had other singleton free-ish licenses in the past as well as many proprietary licenses for \"Adobe typefaces.\" It seems to me like _this_ license needs an identifier to distinguish it from the other two Utopia licenses as well. I don't know who would be regarded as the steward; perhaps Adobe or the X Consortium.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1718945814/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1719539600","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2121#issuecomment-1719539600","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2121","id":1719539600,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85mfheQ","user":{"login":"karsten-klein","id":20038021,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDM4MDIx","avata