ollowers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n8willis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n8willis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n8willis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n8willis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n8willis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n8willis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n8willis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n8willis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-09-14T15:39:32Z","updated_at":"2023-09-14T15:39:32Z","body":"> At the core it is a misformatted BSD-3 Clause variant with reduced disclaimer:\r\n\r\nWe must be seeing different things for some reason, because it does not look quite so similar to me. In particular, the original Adobe license does not address modification (which was the point of contention with Debian back at the time).\r\n\r\n> At the end an additional terms are mentioned: \"You are free to do whatever you please with scanners generated using flex; for them, you are not even bound by the above copyright.\"\r\n\r\nI'm also not seeing this. Can you link to this line?\r\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1719696014/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1719799042","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2121#issuecomment-1719799042","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2121","id":1719799042,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85mgg0C","user":{"login":"karsten-klein","id":20038021,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDM4MDIx","avatar_url":"https://av